Revised GSPR 14.1:

"The device shall incorporate a passive UHF RFID transponder (ISO/IEC 18000-63 Type C / EPC Gen2v2) embedded within the handle polymer matrix, demonstrating:

a) Read-range ≥ 3 m through sterile barrier system (ISO 11607-1 validated packaging) at 2 W ERP;
b) Functional survival post-sterilization per ISO 11135 (EO: 55°C, 600 mg/L, 4 hr) AND ISO 17665 (steam: 134°C, 3.5 min) — manufacturer to declare validated cycle;
c) Unique Device Identifier (UDI) carrier per MDR Art. 27 / 2019/2075, GS1 Application Identifier (01) + (21) encoded in EPC memory bank 01h;
d) Biocompatibility per ISO 10993-1 evaluation — tag materials covered by device Master File;
e) Electromagnetic compatibility per IEC 60601-1-2:2014 + AMD1:2020, emissions Class B, immunity test level 3.

Verification: Accelerated aging (ASTM F1980) + RFID read verification at T0, T12, T24 months. Documentation per Annex II/III technical file."

Next: GSPR 17 — single-use claim justification.
